 or bloodraven his  real name is Brendan rivers and guess  what he's actually related to maester  aemon and Rhaegar Targaryen and  course John Snow the three-eyed Raven is  a bastard Targaryen he's actually made  up of ice and fire just like John Snow  his father was a Targaryen and his  mother was a Blackwood which is a  descendant of the first men some of you  may not know this but the three-eyed  Raven actually joined the Nights Watch  the same exact day maester aemon did in  fact they traveled to the wall together  considering they were related they must  have had a close relationship with each  other Wow at the wall together shortly  after they joined the Nights Watch  the three-eyed Raven actually became the  Lord Commander at Castle black and his  maester was Aemon Targaryen and I'm sure  they gave each other counsel as much as  possible the three-eyed Raven was the  Lord Commander for over 10 years so  these two had to have spent an awful lot  of time together and they must have  formed a strong Alliance together  considering they did have to look out  for each other at the wall like all men  of the Nights Watch should the only  problem is it's not actually known when  the three-eyed Raven started getting his  greenseer abilities but it was well  known that he was into all kinds of  sorcery and the dark arts before he  joined the Nights Watch  so Amon most likely knew he was into  some creepy [ __ ]  but the three-eyed Raven eventually ends  up going missing from Castle black no  one knows where he went or what happened  to him but he may have kept in contact  with maester aemon  now I'm not saying maester aemon knew he  was stuck in the tree the whole time but  the three-eyed raven could have been  sending maester aemon some information  without him even knowing it was coming  from him maester aemon was the one who  took care of the Ravens at Castle black  and there is evidence from the books  that hem said Bloodraven actually  speaking through those Ravens and he  could have spoke with Amon through  dreams just like he did with Bryan it's  kind of interesting that Maester Aemon  and the three-eyed raven both had  something happened to their eyes maester  aemon went blind and bloodraven lost an  eye part of the weirwood tree was  actually growing through his eye socket  I also find it interesting that maester  aemon was able to survive for so long  especially in a place as harsh and cruel  as the wall he was the oldest living man  in Westeros and it makes me wonder if  something or someone was keeping him  alive long enough to serve us  cific purpose he did live long enough to  meet John snow and give him some good  counsel and some of the things maester  aemon said to John snow makes me  question how much he actually knew about  him and the bigger picture most  importantly the survival of the realm  maester aemon was well aware of the  azure Ahai prophecy and he actually  spoke about this with Rhaegar Targaryen  maester aemon and Rhaegar used to  discuss who they thought azor Ahai would  be in Rhaegar told maester aemon that  azor Ahai would be one of his sons you  also have to wonder what made Rhaegar so  obsessed with this prophecy what kind of  insight did he have that led him to  believe that it would have to be his son  who would go on to lead the fight  against the darkness could Rhaegar  Targaryen have had prophetic dreams that  told him this and was it the three-eyed  raven who was manipulating those dreams  you have to keep in mind that all these  characters share the same blood the  blood of the Dragon aiment Rhaegar the  three-eyed raven and john are all  connected through their blood there is  also some evidence of the three-eyed  raven helping john on more than one  occasion one way he was helping him was  through his direwolf ghost in the books  that was actually ghost who found the  dragon glass and the Horn of winter  ghost made John follow him and he leads  him right to where it's buried in who do  you think put that stuff there in the  first place  it also should be noted that there are  only a few characters in this story who  have red eyes and ghosts and Bloodraven  are two of those characters I think  that's just another hint as to who  actually sent the Starks there  direwolves they obviously didn't stumble  across those by accident John also notes  that his eyes look like weirwood eyes  and they belonged to the old gods of the  north also blood Bravin actually helps  John get elected as the Lord Commander  of the Nights Watch and we know that  maester aemon voted for John Snow  himself whenever they vote on who's  going to be the next Lord Commander they  had this big giant kettle that they used  to cast their votes and when they used  it they opened it up and a raven flew  out and it landed right next to John and  it said snow then it said snow a few  more times than  right on Jon's shoulder and everyone  notices it was Lord Commander Mormont's  Raven when that happened along with all  the votes that Jon received it pretty  much sealed the deal for who would be  the new Lord Commander there was no  doubt in my mind that was bloodraven  making the Raven say snow and landing on  Jon's shoulder right when they were  trying to decide who should lead Castle  black there is also evidence that  suggests Bloodraven knows Jon as the  king as well he also uses the Raven and  makes it say King right the Jon Snow's  face and he does this as Jon and Lord  Commander Mormont are talking about  Targaryen Kings this is also not a  coincidence at that time Lord Commander  Mormont is telling Jon about maester  aemon and his family's history and he  tells Jon about all the most recent  Targaryen Kings then he says Jaime  Lannister killed the last Dragon King  but right as he says that the Raven  looks right at John and says King which  indicates Jamie did not kill the last  Dragon King because Mormont is looking  at the last Dragon King as he speaks and  that is Jon Snow in the television show  we know for a fact that Bloodraven knows  about Jon because he shows bran division  but there is more than enough evidence  in the box that shows blood Raven is  keeping his eye on Jon and he is  assisting him whenever he can and it's  no secret that maester aemon favors Jon  Snow he grows very close to Jon almost  immediately and some of the things he  says to John or about Jon make me wonder  what Amon might have known about him or  his purpose even if maester aemon didn't  know Jon was a king he may have known  Bloodraven was keeping an eye on him and  that alone would let Amon know that he  was very important when Stannis and  Melisandre show up at the wall they are  both claiming that Stannis is azor Ahai  reborn and they basically put on a show  Stannis pulls out his sword that  Melisandre named Lightbringer and she  has even done something through this  sword to make it glow maester aemon  might have been blind but he saw right  through their [ __ ] immediately  maester aemon knew that Stannis was not  azor Ahai and he knew that his sword was  not light bringer Amon knows that light  bringer would have had some kind of heat  coming off  of it and Stannis's sword is cold steel  the only reason why is sword would glow  is because Melisandre has done some kind  of magic or spell to make the sword glow  red and orange now in the television  show maester aemon actually dies when  he's at the wall but that's not where he  dies in the books when sam leaves the  wall for Old Town to become a maester he  takes maester aemon with him Jon made  sure that maester aemon got out of there  because he had a good feeling that  Melisandre would burn him because of his  Kings blood unfortunately maester aemon  dies anyway he never actually makes it  the old town but maester aemon does do a  few interesting things before he leaves  before Amon leaves for Old Town he says  one last thing - Jon Snow he gives him  one last piece of advice maester aemon  touches Jon's face and he says you are  half the age that egg was in your own  burden is a crueler one I fear you will  have little joy of your command but I  think you have the strength in you to do  the things that must be done kill the  boy Jon Snow winter is almost upon us  kill the boy and let the man be born  maester aemon gave this same speech to  Aegon Targaryen right as he became king  of the Seven Kingdoms there is a very  interesting parallel here because as we  know Jon Snow is Aegon Targaryen as well  and when maester aemon feels Jon's face  Aegon is the first person he thinks of  the other cool parallel was maester  aemon and Rhaegar both thought that an  Aegon would be azor Ahai reborn they had  the right name but they just had two  wrong  Aegon at the time but there is one other  thing maester aemon does before he  leaves Castle black he leaves a book  behind in Jon's chambers and he tells  him to check out the book because he  marked a specific page he wanted John to  read eventually John does read the  passage that maester aemon left for him  and can you guess what it's about it's  about azor Ahai in his burning sword  Lightbringer  now you could say maester aemon wanted  John to read that so he knew Stannis was  a pretender or maybe maester aemon was  trying to get John to see something in  himself since maester aemon is dead we  will never know  exactly why he left that for John to  read after Amon left that book behind he  heads the old town was Sam and he finds  out about Daenerys and her dragons and  he suddenly thinks he has had the  prophecy wrong the whole time he thinks  he was a fool for thinking that azor  Ahai would be a man because it is now  known that Daenerys was the one who woke  dragons from stone but I think maester  aemon had it right the first time it  seems like it's obviously Daenerys  because she fits the prophecy in a  literal sense but I don't think George  will make it that straightforward too  many people within this story are saying  it's Dany which makes me think it won't  be her because that's what we're led to  believe but the answer will be written  between the lines in a dance with  dragons John does have a dream and he  sees himself standing on top of the wall  and he's armored and black ice with a  burning red sword in his hand  I think this dream will eventually  become a reality after he rises from the  dead and it doesn't just suggest that  John will carry Lightbringer  but it's also another hint at John's  Targaryen blood in the dream he is  armored in black with a red sword which  symbolizes the Targaryen colors now when  trying to decide whether a manu about  john or not is tricky because there are  some hints that point at him knowing and  not knowing maester aemon was on record  saying that Daenerys was the last  Targaryen but you would also have to  wonder if Amon had some kind of  motivation to keep the truth about John  a secret like I said earlier even if a  maan didn't know John was a Targaryen  he might have still had knowledge of his  importance other than just being a good  leader he may have had his own  suspicions that bloodraven was keeping  an eye on him but he may have also known  for a fact because he still could have  been in contact with bloodraven through  dreams or through the Ravens themselves  I think one major motivating factor to  keep this a secret is because of how  this could affect the rest of the story  I'm sure all of you remember the scene  when Bloodraven told brand that the ink  was dry he couldn't change things that  happened in the past well I think a  similar thing could be said for the  present time if a mole knew something  about John he might have had to keep  this a secret so it didn't cause any  kind of  effect in the timeline there is a good  chance that bloodraven knows exactly how  things will play out but in order for  that to happen things need to follow a  specific order events cannot be changed  John cannot find out about his 